# Fetched source, cmake trees, and the libraries themselves. Nothing built belongs in git:
# the point of this repo is that the *release assets* are the artifacts, and a committed .a
# is one nobody can tell apart from the one CI made.
build/
dist/
.DS_Store

# The same rule, applied to the Rust half. `prebuilt/` is a cache: ./sync-prebuilt.sh fills
# it from dist/, and failing that crates/fdk-aac-prebuilt-sys/build.rs downloads what it
# needs from the latest release. Nothing about which bytes are correct is stored here —
# that travels with the archives, as SHA256SUMS and each archive's own MANIFEST.
crates/fdk-aac-prebuilt-sys/prebuilt/
target/
Cargo.lock

# Per-checkout notes for Claude Code: which machine has Docker, how to reach it, what its
# shell does differently. All of it is true of one developer's setup rather than of the
# project; anything that holds for everyone belongs in a committed CLAUDE.md instead.
CLAUDE.local.md

# Written by fdk-aac-e2e when it runs. The pipeline uploads it per target and the
# `bit-exact` job compares the four; a copy from whichever machine last ran the binary is
# not a fact about the repository.
digests.txt
